-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Fourth Term Mixed Close Left Front Scalar
-- statement:
--   **The mixed fourth-term expression is within the self-consistency square root of the left-front scalar.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized and assume complete G self consistency at level `zeta`. The difference between the right-tensor and left-tensor versions of the fourth-term sum, averaged over uniform slice-pair questions and all polynomial/outcome pairs, is at most
--
--   $$
--   \left|T_{4,\mathrm{left}}-T_{4,\mathrm{right}}\right|\le\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   Both terms use the complete-part total, the `M` outcome, and the family outcome twice; only the register placement of the family factor changes. This is the named left-front restatement of the second square-root self-consistency step.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateFourthTerm_mixed_close_left_front_scalar`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
